Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>google</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-format</category> <category>okf</category> <category>temporal</category> <category>trust</category> <description>Google&#39;s Open Knowledge Format standardises content packaging for agents but stops before trust, temporality, and governance. KCP covers exactly that territory.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/17/googles-open-knowledge-format-and-the-problems-it-deliberately-doesnt-solve/</link> <pubDate>Wed, 17 Jun 2026 18:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/17/googles-open-knowledge-format-and-the-problems-it-deliberately-doesnt-solve/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Sixteen Versions of Metadata Nobody Read</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>compound-developer</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>practitioner-notes</category> <category>regulatory-compliance</category> <category>synthesis</category> <category>temporal</category> <category>verification</category> <description>63 regulatory manifests with full KCP v0.21 metadata -- hashes, signatures, temporal validity. Then a benchmark showed agents were not reading any of it.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/14/sixteen-versions-of-metadata-nobody-read/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 14 Jun 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/14/sixteen-versions-of-metadata-nobody-read/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Discoverable Is Not Navigable</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>ExoCortex</category> <category>agentic-writing</category> <category>agents-reading</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-infrastructure</category> <category>meta</category> <category>sdd</category> <description>Discoverable is not navigable. Extracting 38 Dutch obligation units from inline YAML to standalone text made content agent-traversable, not just findable.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/14/discoverable-is-not-navigable/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 14 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/14/discoverable-is-not-navigable/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Stale Knowledge Is Worse Than No Knowledge: KCP v0.19 and v0.20 Close the Temporal Gap</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-context</category> <category>bi-temporal</category> <category>compliance</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>temporal</category> <description>Stale knowledge is worse than none. KCP v0.19 adds bi-temporal validity and supersession links; v0.20 adds as_of queries for point-in-time compliance.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/stale-knowledge-is-worse-than-no-knowledge-kcp-v019-and-v020-close-the-temporal-gap/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 17:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/stale-knowledge-is-worse-than-no-knowledge-kcp-v019-and-v020-close-the-temporal-gap/</guid> </item> <item> <title>2026 06 12 kcp 0.18 unit integrity</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-security</category> <category>content-integrity</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>supply-chain-security</category> <category>trust</category> <description>KCP v0.18 adds per-unit content hashes and origin evidence. Signing the manifest proves the map is authentic; hashes prove the territory matches.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/2026-06-12-kcp-018-unit-integrity/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/2026-06-12-kcp-018-unit-integrity/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Down the Rabbit Hole: How a 33-Tool-Call Bug Became a Knowledge Standard</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>compliance</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-context-protocol</category> <category>mcp</category> <category>open-source</category> <category>sdd</category> <category>skill-driven-development</category> <category>trust</category> <description>KCP started when a 33-tool-call bug revealed agents waste their budget on discovery. Six months later: a knowledge standard with trust and governance.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/down-the-rabbit-hole-how-a-33-tool-call-bug-became-a-knowledge-standard/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 11:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/down-the-rabbit-hole-how-a-33-tool-call-bug-became-a-knowledge-standard/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Beyond RAG: How KCP 0.16--0.17 Give Agents Trustworthy, Self-Describing Knowledge</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-security</category> <category>content-structure</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>mcp</category> <category>rag</category> <category>trust</category> <description>KCP v0.16 adds cryptographic signing and trust tiers. v0.17 adds content structure metadata and subtractive audience filtering for precision retrieval.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/beyond-rag-how-kcp-016--017-give-agents-trustworthy-self-describing-knowledge/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 12 Jun 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/12/beyond-rag-how-kcp-016--017-give-agents-trustworthy-self-describing-knowledge/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Explorative Development</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Skill-Driven Development</category> <category>agentic-engineering</category> <category>ai-productivity</category> <category>compound-developer</category> <category>explorative-development</category> <category>fear-driven-development</category> <category>hypothesis-driven</category> <category>practitioner-notes</category> <category>simulation</category> <category>verification</category> <description>Before writing production code, run a fictional organisation through two years of using the feature. Front-load discovery before the first commit.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/explorative-development/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 11 Jun 2026 18:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/explorative-development/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Organized Truths</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Skill-Driven Development</category> <category>agentic-engineering</category> <category>ai-productivity</category> <category>compound-developer</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-infrastructure</category> <category>practitioner-notes</category> <category>regulatory-compliance</category> <category>verification</category> <description>Catch an agent making a false compliance claim once, encode the verification as a skill, and every future session inherits the check. Organised truths scale.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/organized-truths/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 11 Jun 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/organized-truths/</guid> </item> <item> <title>False Alarms and False Assurances</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Skill-Driven Development</category> <category>agentic-engineering</category> <category>ai-productivity</category> <category>code-review</category> <category>compound-developer</category> <category>fear-driven-development</category> <category>practitioner-notes</category> <category>verification</category> <description>An agent claimed an API had no authentication. Four minutes of reading proved otherwise. Verifying agent assertions is the non-negotiable skill.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/false-alarms-and-false-assurances/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 11 Jun 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/11/false-alarms-and-false-assurances/</guid> </item> <item> <title>The Compound Developer</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Skill-Driven Development</category> <category>agentic-engineering</category> <category>ai-productivity</category> <category>compound-developer</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>human-ai-collaboration</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>multi-agent</category> <category>sdd</category> <category>vibe-coding</category> <description>METR found AI made experienced developers 19% slower. The compound developer -- with persistent context infrastructure -- proves architecture matters more.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/02/the-compound-developer/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 02 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/02/the-compound-developer/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Everyone Is Auditing the Workflow. Nobody Is Fixing the Knowledge.</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-governance</category> <category>architecture</category> <category>audit</category> <category>compliance</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>nolta</category> <category>provenance</category> <description>Everyone audits the AI workflow. Nobody fixes the knowledge feeding it. Without typed, signed units, audit trails record that review happened but not what.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/01/everyone-is-auditing-the-workflow-nobody-is-fixing-the-knowledge/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jun 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/01/everyone-is-auditing-the-workflow-nobody-is-fixing-the-knowledge/</guid> </item> <item> <title>The Law Is Also Knowledge. Package It.</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-governance</category> <category>audit</category> <category>compliance</category> <category>eu-ai-act</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>nis2</category> <category>provenance</category> <category>regulations</category> <description>Regulations are knowledge. KCP types them as versioned packages with temporal validity and cryptographic binding -- compliance becomes evaluable, not anecdotal.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/01/the-law-is-also-knowledge-package-it/</link> <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jun 2026 09:30:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/06/01/the-law-is-also-knowledge-package-it/</guid> </item> <item> <title>From Policy to Practice: How KCP Makes Regulations Machine-Readable for AI Agents</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>ai-agents</category> <category>architecture</category> <category>audit</category> <category>compliance</category> <category>gdpr</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>regulations</category> <description>KCP packages regulations as typed, versioned knowledge units so AI agents can apply GDPR, NIS2, and the EU AI Act at the point of decision, not after the fact.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/30/from-policy-to-practice-how-kcp-makes-regulations-machine-readable-for-ai-agents/</link> <pubDate>Sat, 30 May 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/30/from-policy-to-practice-how-kcp-makes-regulations-machine-readable-for-ai-agents/</guid> </item> <item> <title>The Beginning</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>aegis</category> <category>lib-pcb</category> <category>methodology</category> <category>origin-story</category> <category>sdd</category> <category>skills</category> <category>synthesis</category> <description>How a PCB library, a knowledge system, and a naming conversation became a brand -- eXOReaction&#39;s practice growing distinct enough to need its own identity.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/12/the-beginning/</link> <pubDate>Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/12/the-beginning/</guid> </item> <item> <title>The Harness Before the Service</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <author>Claude Code</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>Agent Infrastructure</category> <category>aegis</category> <category>agent-harness</category> <category>anthropic</category> <category>claude-code</category> <category>exocortex</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>managed-agents</category> <category>synthesis</category> <description>Anthropic&#39;s Managed Agents ship orchestration, supervision, and lifecycle management. The same structural pattern emerged independently in the ExoCortex stack.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/10/the-harness-before-the-service/</link> <pubDate>Sun, 10 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/10/the-harness-before-the-service/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Why KCP Is Passive Data, Not Executable Config — And Why That Matters Now</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>KCP</category> <category>Security</category> <category>agent-config</category> <category>claude-md</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-yaml</category> <category>mcp</category> <category>passive-data</category> <category>security</category> <category>trustfall</category> <description>TrustFall showed why executable config in repos is dangerous. KCP is passive data by design -- manifests declare knowledge structure but never execute anything.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/08/why-kcp-is-passive-data-not-executable-config--and-why-that-matters-now/</link> <pubDate>Fri, 08 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/08/why-kcp-is-passive-data-not-executable-config--and-why-that-matters-now/</guid> </item> <item> <title>Making Ægis Machine-Readable in One Session</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>AI Engineering</category> <category>KCP</category> <category>aegis</category> <category>ed25519</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-yaml</category> <category>llms-txt</category> <category>signing</category> <description>An AI-era consulting company that is not machine-readable is invisible to half the evaluation pipeline. One session to add KCP manifests and structured data.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/07/making-%C3%A6gis-machine-readable-in-one-session/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 07 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/07/making-%C3%A6gis-machine-readable-in-one-session/</guid> </item> <item> <title>How Agents Navigate the Agentic Web</title> <author>Thor Henning Hetland</author> <category>AI-Augmented Development</category> <category>KCP</category> <category>Knowledge Infrastructure</category> <category>agentic-web</category> <category>cantara</category> <category>ed25519</category> <category>federation</category> <category>github-actions</category> <category>kcp</category> <category>knowledge-yaml</category> <category>llms-txt</category> <category>open-source</category> <category>signing</category> <description>How agents navigate repos depends on what is there to find. 157 repositories reveal the gap between discoverable, navigable, and actually useful knowledge.</description> <link>https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/07/how-agents-navigate-the-agentic-web/</link> <pubDate>Thu, 07 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate> <source url="https://wiki.totto.org/feed_rss_created.xml">Thor Henning Hetland</source><guid isPermaLink="true">https://wiki.totto.org/blog/2026/05/07/how-agents-navigate-the-agentic-web/</guid> </item> </channel> </rss>